    {%- comment -%}
      INH Verified unknown-path guard (go-live, approved 2026-09-29). Any path under
      /pages/sauna-database/ that is not an ACTIVE model page falls through to the hub page.
      There: noindex, no canonical, no structured data. The real hub and every other page
      are unchanged. Never noindex together with a canonical.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign inhv_unknown_path = false
      if template.suffix == 'inh-verified-hub'
        assign inhv_segs = request.path | split: 'pages/sauna-database/'
        if inhv_segs.size > 1
          assign inhv_unknown_path = true
        endif
      endif
    -%}
    {%- if inhv_unknown_path %}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    {%- else %}
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Round 14 #10. Every if/endif block in this chain left a newline in the
      rendered <title> — homepage "…Tubs\n\n – inhousewellness\n", collection
      "…Filled\n\n\n" — on EVERY branch, predating Round 12. Google collapses
      whitespace, so this was cosmetic; the measured decoded lengths do not change.

      The chain is captured and whitespace is collapsed ONCE at output. split: ' '
      is Ruby's awk-style split (any whitespace run, empties dropped), so the join
      is the same collapse the length measurement applies. No branch logic changed.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture title_tag_text -%}
      {%- if collection -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Was `{{ collection.title }}` plus a shop-name suffix, which IGNORED the SEO title
          field. 52 collection SEO titles were written, applied and confirmed set via the
          Admin API in September 2026, and not one reached the page.

          `page_title` resolves to the SEO title when set and falls back to collection.title
          when not, so collections without a written title are unaffected.

          The shop-name suffix is dropped ONLY where an SEO title exists: those 52 are
          measured at <=60 decoded characters and already carry the brand where it fits.
          Appending 18 more would truncate every one. Collections with no SEO title keep
          the previous behaviour, suffix included.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {{ page_title }}
        {%- if paginate.current_page > 1 %} – Page {{ paginate.current_page }}{% endif %}
        {%- if collection.metafields.global.title_tag == blank %} – {{ shop.name }}{% endif %}
      {%- elsif current_tags and current_tags.size > 0 -%}
        Sauna Blog: {{ current_tags | join: ', ' }} Insights
        {%- if paginate.current_page > 1 %} – Page {{ paginate.current_page }}{% endif %}
        – {{ shop.name }}
      {%- elsif article -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Articles get NO shop-name suffix. It costs 18 characters of a ~60-character
          SERP budget, and 109 of 112 article titles rendered over 60 characters with it
          attached — they were being truncated by Google. Removing it puts 74 of 112
          under the limit. Blog pages produce 89% of this site's organic clicks, so this
          is the single highest-leverage title change available.

          Deliberately scoped to `article` only. Collection, product, page and blog-listing
          titles keep the suffix; their lengths have not been measured and should not be
          changed on the strength of article data.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {{ page_title }}
        {%- if paginate.current_page > 1 %} – Page {{ paginate.current_page }}{% endif %}
      {%- elsif product -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Products get NO shop-name suffix, for the reason Round 3a gave for articles
          and DEFERRED for products: their lengths had not been measured.

          Measured 10 September 2026 across 481 ACTIVE products, decoded:
            with the suffix     438 of 481 over 60 characters   median 84
            without the suffix  317 of 481 over 60 characters   median 66
          The suffix is 18 characters of a ~60-character SERP budget and clears 121.

          It is NOT a solution. 317 titles remain over 60 because most product titles
          are long on their own — the outdoor-kitchen titles run past 100 characters
          bare. This is the cheapest 18 characters, nothing more.

          Added as its own `elsif` AHEAD of the else rather than editing the else.
          That else is a CATCH-ALL: it also serves the homepage, static pages, blog
          index pages, search and 404. Editing it would strip the suffix from all of
          them on a measurement taken only on products — the exact mistake Round 3a's
          comment warns about. Their lengths remain unmeasured, so they are unchanged.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {{ page_title }}
        {%- if paginate.current_page > 1 %} – Page {{ paginate.current_page }}{% endif %}
      {%- elsif metaobject -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          INH Verified model pages (Round 2): the title tag is exactly the SEO title,
          "[Title]: Verified Specs & Electrical Requirements", with no shop-name suffix.
          Scoped to metaobject pages only; every other branch is unchanged.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {{ page_title }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ page_title }}
        {%- if paginate.current_page > 1 %} – Page {{ paginate.current_page }}{% endif %}
        {%- unless page_title contains shop.name %} – {{ shop.name }}{% endunless %}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture %}
    <title>{{ title_tag_text | split: ' ' | join: ' ' }}</title>
    {%- if current_tags and current_tags.size > 0 -%}
      <meta
        name="description"
        content="Explore expert articles on {{ current_tags | join: ', ' }} in our sauna & wellness blog. Discover infrared, traditional, and hybrid sauna insights.{% if paginate.current_page > 1 %} – Page {{ paginate.current_page }}{% endif %}"
      >
    {%- elsif template contains 'collection' -%}
      <meta
        name="description"
        content="{% if paginate.current_page > 1 %}Page {{ paginate.current_page }} of our collection. {% endif %}{% if page_description != blank %}{{ page_description | escape }}{% elsif collection.description != blank %}{{ collection.description | strip_html | truncate: 155 }}{% else %}Shop our curated wellness collection including saunas, cold plunges, and more.{% endif %}"
      >
    {%- elsif page_description -%}
      <meta
        name="description"
        content="{{ page_description | escape }}{% if paginate.current_page > 1 %} – Page {{ paginate.current_page }}{% endif %}"
      >
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Added 2026-09-09. Without this branch a page with no page_description
        rendered NO <meta name="description"> at all — not a bad one, none.
        That was 8 blog indexes, 4 pages and 48 products.

        It went unnoticed because snippets/meta-tags.liquid ALREADY has this
        fallback for og:description, so social previews looked correct while the
        search-facing tag was absent. A partial safety net on an adjacent tag
        makes the gap invisible to anyone checking casually.

        THIS DOES NOT REPLACE WRITING REAL METAS. It stops the floor being zero.
        The 48 products without one still need real descriptions — see BACKLOG.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <meta
        name="description"
        content="{{ shop.description | default: shop.name | escape }}{% if paginate.current_page > 1 %} – Page {{ paginate.current_page }}{% endif %}"
      >
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Round 8. The Wellness Institute blog is a RESOURCE LIBRARY — source material
      supporting articles published elsewhere on the site. Client ruling 10 Sep 2026:
      noindex it, per page, rather than canonical. A canonical asserts two pages are
      the same thing, and source material and the synopsis it supports are not.

      `follow` is deliberate: the pages stay crawlable so the links they carry to
      their parents still pass.

      firepit-safety is EXCLUDED. It earns 411 impressions at position 12.68 while
      its parent earns zero, and noindexing it does not hand those impressions over.
      The parent is the problem and it is in the 329 unread. Revisit after the parent
      is fixed — see reports/institute-blog.md.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      # `article.handle` is not reliably populated in the LAYOUT, so
      # `article.handle != 'firepit-safety'` evaluated nil != string = TRUE and
      # noindexed the one page that must stay indexed. Caught on the preview, not
      # in review. request.path is populated here and is what the exclusion uses.
      assign robots_noindex = false
      if blog.handle == 'institute'
        assign robots_noindex = true
        if request.path contains 'firepit-safety'
          assign robots_noindex = false
        endif
      endif
      # current_tags LAST so a filtered view is always noindexed, whatever else ran.
      if current_tags
        assign robots_noindex = true
      endif
    -%}
    {% if robots_noindex %}
      <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
    {% endif %}
    {% render 'meta-tags' %}
    {%- comment -%}
      BreadcrumbList on every non-index page, and CollectionPage + ItemList on the
      collections that have copy. Round 7. Product breadcrumbs are built from
      product.collections, NOT from the `collection` global, which is blank on the
      canonical product URL Google indexes.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- unless inhv_unknown_path %}{% render 'structured-data-extras' %}{% endunless %}
    {%- comment -%}
      Round 14. Organization node, HOMEPAGE ONLY, tested positively on template.name
      (populated in the layout — the VideoObject block above relies on it).

      Every value is client-confirmed, 15 Sep 2026, and every URL was resolved
      before shipping:
        name / url / logo        the storefront and settings.logo
        contactPoint             support@ is the public contact (help@ is warranty claims only)
        address                  the business location. NOT a returns address, and nothing
                                 about returns belongs in markup. #20752 is the suite on every
                                 PUBLISHED page and on the Facebook page; #21140 survives only
                                 on four unpublished pages; the billing address is not public.
        sameAs                   Facebook page 61569426503966 in its canonical people/ form
                                 (the footer links the same page as profile.php?id=); the other
                                 four from the footer. YouTube is the channel, not its /shorts tab.
      Fields NOT confirmed are omitted, not guessed: founder, foundingDate.
      Round 15: telephone confirmed from the footer and added. aggregateRating is sourced from
      shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_rating / all_reviews_count — never hardcoded, so it
      cannot go stale.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if template.name == 'index' -%}
      <script type="application/ld+json">
        {
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "InHouse Wellness",
          "url": "{{ shop.url }}/",
          {%- if settings.logo != blank %}
          "logo": "https:{{ settings.logo | image_url: width: 600 }}",
          {%- endif %}
          "telephone": "+1-512-559-8860",
          "contactPoint": {
            "@type": "ContactPoint",
            "contactType": "customer support",
            "email": "support@inhousewellness.com",
            "telephone": "+1-512-559-8860"
          },
          "address": {
            "@type": "PostalAddress",
            "streetAddress": "5900 Balcones Drive #20752",
            "addressLocality": "Austin",
            "addressRegion": "TX",
            "postalCode": "78731",
            "addressCountry": "US"
          },
          {%- liquid
            assign shop_rating = shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_rating.value | plus: 0.0
            assign shop_reviews = shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_count.value | plus: 0
          -%}
          {%- if shop_reviews > 0 and shop_rating > 0 %}
          "aggregateRating": {
            "@type": "AggregateRating",
            "ratingValue": {{ shop_rating }},
            "bestRating": 5,
            "worstRating": 1,
            "reviewCount": {{ shop_reviews }}
          },
          {%- endif %}
          "sameAs": [
            "https://www.facebook.com/people/InHouse-Wellness/61569426503966/",
            "https://www.instagram.com/inhouse.wellness/",
            "https://www.tiktok.com/@inhousewellness",
            "https://www.youtube.com/@InHouseWellness",
            "https://www.pinterest.com/inhousewellness/"
          ]
        }
      </script>
    {%- endif -%}
